{"change_summary":"Extracted the duplicated conservation scenario setup into a shared `tank_core::test_fixtures` module and rewired both `crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs` and `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_conservation.rs` to import the same grazing, feeding, mortality/senescence, trim, water-change, gas-exchange, DIC-shortcut, and trace-dump helpers. I also tightened the mortality/senescence coverage in both suites by asserting that `system:daily_shrimp` records both adult-count loss and a positive `detritus.fine_g` delta, so shrimp death -> detritus routing is now verified explicitly instead of only inferred from end-state counts.","outstanding_risks":[],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the two conservation suites to confirm the duplicated fixture/helpers and identify the missing shrimp-death trace assertion in the mortality scenario.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Added `crates/tank_core/src/test_fixtures.rs`, exported it from `tank_core`, updated both test files to use the shared fixtures/trace helper, and added explicit `system:daily_shrimp` -> `detritus.fine_g` routing assertions in the mortality scenario paths.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting and the targeted conservation regression/e2e suites to verify the shared fixtures compile cleanly and the strengthened mortality assertions pass.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo fmt --all --check` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test conservation_regression -- --nocapture` passed: 6 tests passed, 0 failed.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_conservation -- --nocapture` passed: 1 test passed, 0 failed; the summary reported all 6 scenarios as PASS.","The e2e summary still reports zero closed-system drift within tolerance and the expected open-system deltas, including `trim_and_remove` at `dN=-38.500000000 mg`, `dC=-240.625000000 mg`, and `water_change` at `dN=+21.187500000 mg`, `dC=+97.500000000 mg`."]}